This module contains azure compute and networking services. It serves as an outline on the services you can get from azure.

Azure virtual machines.
As we shoul already know, a virtual machine is a virtual occurance of a physical computer. You can configure
an operating system, run tasks, configure network access, access files, browse the web, etc.
Virtual machines are provided as an Iaas. 
You can run custom software, use custom configurations and gives access to the whole OS.
It being an Iaas deployed service, you need to manage updates on the v.m yourself.
You can deploy VMs in minutes using images. 
An image is a template of a virtul machine that can be loaded when needed instead of recreating a new vm to run
software that is already available as an image.

Scale in VMs
You can run single vms for minor tasks such as testing and development, or you can run multiple vms to provide
redundancy, high availability and scalability. You can manage multiple vms using scale sets and availability sets.

Scale sets
Scale sets allow you to manage a group of identical load balanced vms as a single unit. When deploying a scale set, azure automatically
deploys a load balancer. They can be configured to increase or decrase based on demand. 

Availability sets
Availability sets are deployed for fault tolerance and updates. They are divided into falut domains and update domains.
Fault domains prevent an outage of the entire scale set by segmenting the virtual machines.
Update domains are used for rolling udates, instaed of updating whole vms at once, they update in intervals to preserve haigh availability.

